The code will generate two Assert statements in the PUT_ContainsContract method. The first one checks that if "New_Ret" is false or true, the index of the last occurrence of "x" in "Old_arrList", which is less than or equal to "New_arrList" occurrence index. And the second assert statement checks that "Old_arrList count" is equal to "New_arrList count" unless the "New_ret" is false.--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == false && Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListIndexOfX);
</code>

The output assert is:
```cs
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == false && Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListIndexOfX);
```
So, the assert statement in the context of the test method is stating that the Contains method is supposed to return false if the last index of x in the old arrList is less than or equal to the index of x in the new arrList. This is derived from the comment "If the return value is false, last index of x in old arrList is <= index of x in new arrList".--------------------
Debug.Assert((Old_arrListIndexOfX < 0) || (Old_arrListIndexOfX >= New_arrListIndexOfX));
